WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.266 --> 00:00:00.934 size:88% position:44% line:92%
-Your family. Two girls.

00:00:00.934 --> 00:00:03.003
Halloween. Do you they kno
what they're going to be yet

00:00:03.003 --> 00:00:03.670 line:92%
-Oh, yeah. They do, yeah.

00:00:03.670 --> 00:00:05.071 align:start size:94% position:6%
Hazel's going to be
a rocket ship.

00:00:05.071 --> 00:00:07.073 align:start size:94% position:6%
-A rocket ship?
-Yeah. Like a full rocket --

00:00:07.073 --> 00:00:09.342
I was like, "An astronaut?
She was like, "Rocket ship."

00:00:09.342 --> 00:00:10.443 line:92%
And I was like, "Astronaut."

00:00:10.443 --> 00:00:11.878 align:start size:94% position:6%
She's like, "No, no, no.
It's a rocket ship."

00:00:11.878 --> 00:00:15.682
-Gotcha. Then, is the poin
of the rocket ship the head?

00:00:15.682 --> 00:00:17.117 align:start size:94% position:6%
Is that like --
-Yup. Correct.

00:00:17.117 --> 00:00:19.285 align:start size:94% position:6%
-She's, like, in the cockpit
-Okay, gotcha.

00:00:19.285 --> 00:00:22.622 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah. And then my younges
is going to be a cat.

00:00:22.622 --> 00:00:23.656 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Okay.

00:00:23.656 --> 00:00:26.092 size:81% position:41%
-And I said, you know,
"So what should I be?"

00:00:26.092 --> 00:00:26.760 size:81% position:41% line:92%
And the youngest says,

00:00:26.760 --> 00:00:28.294
"You should be an alien
for Hazel's rocket ship."

00:00:28.294 --> 00:00:30.163 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah, that's very good.
-I said, "Wow. That's so nice.

00:00:30.163 --> 00:00:32.766 size:88% position:44%
Maybe I will be an alien
that has cat ears on."

00:00:32.766 --> 00:00:35.835 align:start size:94% position:6%
And she goes,
"Daddy, I'm the cat."

00:00:35.835 --> 00:00:38.104 size:84% position:42% line:92%
"Okay. Geez. I get it."

00:00:38.104 --> 00:00:40.874 align:start size:94% position:6%
And then she, like,
stabbed me with a Barbie leg

00:00:40.874 --> 00:00:41.841 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
I was like, "Oh."

00:00:41.841 --> 00:00:46.613 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Do you, fellow New Englander,
do you have any good

00:00:46.613 --> 00:00:49.482 align:start size:94% position:6%
Halloween memories
of your days growing up?

00:00:49.482 --> 00:00:50.550 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I have tons.
-Yeah.

00:00:50.550 --> 00:00:51.985 align:start size:94% position:6%
-My birthday
is around Halloween,

00:00:51.985 --> 00:00:53.553 align:start size:94% position:6%
so it was always
that big month for me.

00:00:53.553 --> 00:00:54.821 align:start size:94% position:6%
But do you remember
Spooky World?

00:00:54.821 --> 00:00:56.890 align:start size:94% position:6%
-When it was mentioned to me
today, I have --

00:00:56.890 --> 00:00:59.626 align:start size:94% position:6%
-It was on the radio,
and it was, "Spooky World.

00:00:59.626 --> 00:01:01.361 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Okay.
-Not ringing any bells?

00:01:01.361 --> 00:01:03.363 size:75% position:38%
Now I'm embarrassed.
-But I never went.

00:01:03.363 --> 00:01:06.099
I never went to Spooky World
-It's basically our versio

00:01:06.099 --> 00:01:08.401 align:start size:94% position:6%
of all of the amazing
special effects,

00:01:08.401 --> 00:01:10.470 line:92%
L.A., you know, scare areas.

00:01:10.470 --> 00:01:13.139 align:start size:94% position:6%
So, a guy came to Boston
and started one. Spooky World.

00:01:13.139 --> 00:01:14.908 align:start size:94% position:6%
It's not quite as well done.
-Uh-huh.

00:01:14.908 --> 00:01:16.709 align:start size:94% position:6%
-But it was just
so many good stories,

00:01:16.709 --> 00:01:19.446 align:start size:94% position:6%
one of which was I go throug
the haunted house.

00:01:19.446 --> 00:01:21.548 align:start size:94% position:6%
I'm terrified
of all things scary.

00:01:21.548 --> 00:01:23.016 size:75% position:38%
Is anybody else? No?
You guys are all --

00:01:23.016 --> 00:01:25.351 align:start size:94% position:6%
You're terrifying.
-Was Spooky World in Boston?

00:01:25.351 --> 00:01:27.420 size:81% position:41%
-Oh, no, in the middle
of nowhere, in a farm.

00:01:27.420 --> 00:01:29.122 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Okay, got you.
-And it was terrifying

00:01:29.122 --> 00:01:30.957 align:start size:94% position:6%
and scary,
and they had a haunted house

00:01:30.957 --> 00:01:33.259 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I just loved --
There was one father

00:01:33.259 --> 00:01:35.795
with, like, a 7-year-old boy
going in in front of me in line.

00:01:35.795 --> 00:01:37.430 size:78% position:39%
And the kid was like,
"I want to go in."

00:01:37.430 --> 00:01:38.932 align:start size:94% position:6%
He's like, "You know what?
Let's not go in.

00:01:38.932 --> 00:01:40.567
I think you're too young.
And I think you're scared.

00:01:40.567 --> 00:01:41.768 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I don't think
we should do it."

00:01:41.768 --> 00:01:42.969 align:start size:94% position:6%
And the kid's like,
"No, I'm fine."

00:01:42.969 --> 00:01:44.704 align:start size:94% position:6%
And you could tell
it was definitely the father

00:01:44.704 --> 00:01:46.306 align:start size:94% position:6%
who was terrified.
So, as he's going through,

00:01:46.306 --> 00:01:48.174
he's like, "I don't really
think we should do this.

00:01:48.174 --> 00:01:50.443 align:start size:94% position:6%
I don't know."
So, we got in, and the first

00:01:50.443 --> 00:01:53.246
turn we took is Dracula
coming out of his coffin.

00:01:53.246 --> 00:01:56.349 align:start size:94% position:6%
I kid you not.
The Dracula is like, "Blah!"

00:01:56.349 --> 00:01:57.250 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
And he goes...

00:01:57.250 --> 00:01:59.686 align:start size:94% position:6%
And just --
I mean, hit Dracula.

00:01:59.686 --> 00:02:02.555
And Dracula was like, "No!
And the coffin went back.

00:02:02.555 --> 00:02:05.258 align:start size:94% position:6%
And then, I swear to God,
as we were leaving,

00:02:05.258 --> 00:02:09.028 size:78% position:39%
I saw Dracula talking
to a cop and the guy.

00:02:09.028 --> 00:02:12.165 size:78% position:39%
And Dracula was like,
"And then he hit me.

00:02:12.165 --> 00:02:16.369
It was -- It was fantastic
Worth the price of admission

00:02:16.369 --> 00:02:21.174
-I mean, to see a guy, to see
Massachusetts guy punch Dracula.

00:02:21.174 --> 00:02:22.142 line:92%
That's why they have, like -

00:02:22.142 --> 00:02:24.277 align:start size:94% position:6%
There's almost no reports
of vampires in Massachusetts

00:02:24.277 --> 00:02:26.746 align:start size:94% position:6%
'Cause they're like,
"It's not worth the trouble.

00:02:26.746 --> 00:02:28.381 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah, you'll just
get coldcocked.

00:02:28.381 --> 00:02:29.215 line:92%
-Yeah, you'll get coldcocked

00:02:29.215 --> 00:02:31.618 align:start size:94% position:6%
and also their blood's got
a lot of alcohol in it.

00:02:31.618 --> 00:02:33.820 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah, totally.
-It's mostly beer.

00:02:33.820 --> 00:02:36.055 align:start size:94% position:6%
-You can't bite and drive
in Boston.

00:02:36.055 --> 00:02:37.257 line:92%
-Yeah, no, no, absolutely not.

00:02:37.257 --> 00:02:39.792 size:88% position:44%
You've been name-dropped
a few times on our show

00:02:39.792 --> 00:02:41.361 align:start size:94% position:6%
recently by other guests.
-Really?

00:02:41.361 --> 00:02:42.996 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Which I think
is very high praise.

00:02:42.996 --> 00:02:44.697 align:start size:94% position:6%
-It's great praise.
-Chris Hayes, who --

00:02:44.697 --> 00:02:45.865 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I went to college
with Chris Hayes.

00:02:45.865 --> 00:02:47.734 align:start size:94% position:6%
-You went to college
with Chris Hayes. And you --

00:02:47.734 --> 00:02:50.236 align:start size:94% position:6%
You guys were in the
theater department together.

00:02:50.236 --> 00:02:51.771 align:start size:94% position:6%
-He was in
the theater department,

00:02:51.771 --> 00:02:54.674 size:78% position:39%
and I was just, like,
Armed Guard Number 4

00:02:54.674 --> 00:02:55.842 size:88% position:44% line:92%
in whatever I could get.

00:02:55.842 --> 00:02:57.243 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Was that --
No, so, your early days --

00:02:57.243 --> 00:02:59.312 align:start size:94% position:6%
This is very healthy
for people to hear, I think.

00:02:59.312 --> 00:03:01.114 align:start size:94% position:6%
Especially young actors
in college.

00:03:01.114 --> 00:03:03.349 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I was ready to be a
professional chorus member

00:03:03.349 --> 00:03:04.384 size:81% position:41% line:92%
forever. It was great.

00:03:04.384 --> 00:03:07.420 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Did you guys --
Is it true that you did a --

00:03:07.420 --> 00:03:08.988 line:92%
you did a "Diehard" play?

00:03:08.988 --> 00:03:11.925
-Yes, he directed a play
called "Artistic License."

00:03:11.925 --> 00:03:13.126 line:92%
Brown is an amazing school

00:03:13.126 --> 00:03:16.229 align:start size:94% position:6%
and does all these --
allows you to take big risks

00:03:16.229 --> 00:03:19.332 align:start size:94% position:6%
So we did.
We did "Diehard: The Musical

00:03:19.332 --> 00:03:21.267 line:92%
at Brown, and Chris directed

00:03:21.267 --> 00:03:22.969 align:start size:94% position:6%
And he was
the most amazing director.

00:03:22.969 --> 00:03:27.273 size:88% position:44%
Because I was, you know,
Scared Guest Number 6,

00:03:27.273 --> 00:03:28.408 line:92%
I got to just watch Chris.

00:03:28.408 --> 00:03:30.944
And he had the -- He was
the most intense director.

00:03:30.944 --> 00:03:31.911 size:88% position:44% line:92%
But really enthusiastic.

00:03:31.911 --> 00:03:33.880 align:start size:94% position:6%
So, you'd see him doing this
like this.

00:03:33.880 --> 00:03:39.385
And then whenever somebody had
a nice moment, he would go..

00:03:39.385 --> 00:03:40.320 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:03:40.320 --> 00:03:42.288 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I was like,
"This guy is incredible!"

00:03:42.288 --> 00:03:45.091 align:start size:94% position:6%
But there was an actor,
actually, he was so intense,

00:03:45.091 --> 00:03:46.693 size:78% position:39%
that we -- I remember
we were rehearsing,

00:03:46.693 --> 00:03:48.928 align:start size:94% position:6%
and the sets weren't done yet.
I didn't know that.

00:03:48.928 --> 00:03:51.397 align:start size:94% position:6%
So these sets --
It takes place in the Met.

00:03:51.397 --> 00:03:52.465 line:92%
And so the Temple of Dendur,

00:03:52.465 --> 00:03:54.834 align:start size:94% position:6%
that huge ancient thing
in the Met,

00:03:54.834 --> 00:03:57.103 align:start size:94% position:6%
we had built it
out of Styrofoam.

00:03:57.103 --> 00:03:58.938 align:start size:94% position:6%
But it looked real.
So we rehearsed.

00:03:58.938 --> 00:04:00.506 align:start size:94% position:6%
And our lead actor
goes up there.

00:04:00.506 --> 00:04:02.308 size:88% position:44%
And I actually have this
emblazoned in my brain.

00:04:02.308 --> 00:04:05.044
He started singing the song.
And it was to his daughter

00:04:05.044 --> 00:04:07.313 align:start size:94% position:6%
And he was playing John McClan
or whatever.

00:04:07.313 --> 00:04:08.448 align:start size:94% position:6%
And he goes up on there,
and he goes --

00:04:08.448 --> 00:04:11.251
♪♪ I swore to protect her
and keep her from harm ♪♪

00:04:11.251 --> 00:04:14.854 align:start size:94% position:6%
♪♪ My life gained new meanin
the day she was -- ♪♪

00:04:14.854 --> 00:04:15.388 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
"Ooh! Aah!"

00:04:15.388 --> 00:04:19.092 align:start size:94% position:6%
And he fell a story and a half
through a Styrofoam set.

00:04:19.092 --> 00:04:22.362 line:92%
And I was like, "Oh, my God!

00:04:22.362 --> 00:04:23.796 size:88% position:44% line:92%
And Chris was like this.

00:04:23.796 --> 00:04:25.865 align:start size:94% position:6%
"It's all right!
You're all right!"

00:04:25.865 --> 00:04:28.835 align:start size:94% position:6%
-[ Laughs ]
Early beginnings.

00:04:28.835 --> 00:04:31.671 align:start size:94% position:6%
Early beginnings
to great things.

00:04:31.671 --> 00:04:34.173 size:81% position:41% line:92%
That's John Krasinski.

